cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Svetra in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Svetra: a compiler from a declarative specification to PostgreSQL row-level security, with spec-derived access tests"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aaditya
    family-names: Sinha
version: 0.8.1
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/555aaditya/Svetra"
url: "https://555aaditya.github.io/Svetra/"
abstract: >-
  Svetra compiles a small typed design, svetra.yaml, into a PostgreSQL schema with row-level
  security on every table, TypeScript and Zod types, sign-in settings, and pgTAP access tests
  whose expected results come from evaluating the design itself rather than the generated SQL.
  It explains the design in plain English, shows who can see and change what, and classifies
  every change to the design as safe, breaking or destructive before it reaches the database.
keywords:
  - postgresql
  - row-level security
  - supabase
  - access control
  - compiler
  - testing
  - mutation testing
